# Production builds are SAME-ORIGIN: one Railway service serves both the API and
# this bundle (Decisions, 2026-08-19). Empty, not "/api" — lib/api.js appends /api
# itself, so a base of "/api" would produce /api/api/queue.
#
# This file exists to OVERRIDE a developer web/.env during a production build.
# Vite ranks .env.production above .env, so even a machine with a localhost .env
# cannot compile localhost into a deployed bundle. The failure it prevents is
# silent: the site loads and every request goes to the wrong host.
VITE_API_URL=
